    "sources.caveat.trinka-2015-status-epilepticus": {
      "comment": "Medical sources: caveat of Trinka 2015.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Definiert, ab wann ein Anfall als Status epilepticus behandelt wird (t1); kein Ersatz für den eigenen Notfallplan."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Defines when a seizure is treated as status epilepticus (t1); not a substitute for your own emergency plan."
          }
        },
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Bepaalt vanaf wanneer een aanval als status epilepticus wordt behandeld (t1); geen vervanging van je eigen noodplan."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "발작을 언제 뇌전증지속상태로 치료하는지(t1)를 정의해요. 내 응급 계획을 대신하지는 않아요."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Define cuándo una crisis se considera estado epiléptico (t1); no sustituye a tu propio plan de emergencia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "sources.caveat.nice-ng217-epilepsies": {
      "comment": "Medical sources: caveat of NICE NG217.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Britische Leitlinie; die übliche Dauer plus 2 Minuten gilt für Anfälle mit Zuckungen."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "UK guideline; the usual duration plus 2 minutes applies to convulsive seizures."
          }
        },
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Britse richtlijn; de gebruikelijke duur plus 2 minuten geldt voor convulsieve aanvallen."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "영국 지침이에요. 평소 지속 시간에 2분을 더하는 기준은 경련성 발작에 적용돼요."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Guía del Reino Unido; la duración habitual más 2 minutos se aplica a las crisis convulsivas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "sources.caveat.beniczky-2025-ilae-seizures": {
      "comment": "Medical sources: caveat of the ILAE 2025 classification.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Klassifikation der Anfallsarten; die Einordnung trifft das Behandlungsteam, nicht HealthLog."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Classification of seizure types; the care team classifies, not HealthLog."
          }
        },
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Classificatie van aanvalstypes; het behandelteam deelt in, niet HealthLog."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "발작 유형 분류예요. 분류는 HealthLog가 아니라 의료진이 해요."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Clasificación de los tipos de crisis; clasifica el equipo médico, no HealthLog."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "sources.caveat.cdc-seizure-first-aid": {
      "comment": "Medical sources: caveat of CDC seizure first aid.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Allgemeine Erste-Hilfe-Hinweise; die 5 Minuten gelten, wenn kein eigener Plan vorliegt."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "General first-aid guidance; the 5 minutes apply when there is no plan of your own."
          }
        },
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Algemene eerstehulpadviezen; de 5 minuten gelden als er geen eigen plan is."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "일반 응급처치 안내예요. 5분 기준은 따로 정한 계획이 없을 때 적용돼요."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "Pautas generales de primeros auxilios; los 5 minutos se aplican cuando no hay un plan propio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "sources.method.seizures": {
      "comment": "Medical sources: methodology of the seizure diary thresholds and cluster rules.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Der Timer zeigt den Notfallplan, sobald ein Anfall die Schwelle seiner Anfallsart erreicht: t1 nach Trinka 2015 (tonisch-klonisch 5 Minuten, fokal mit Bewusstseinsstörung und Absence 10 Minuten), bei Anfällen mit Zuckungen die übliche Dauer plus 2 Minuten, wenn das früher ist (NICE NG217), sonst 5 Minuten. Anfallsserien zählen nach deiner Regel und nach NICE (3 in 24 Stunden). Die Anfallsarten folgen der ILAE-Klassifikation 2025."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "The timer shows the emergency plan once a seizure reaches the threshold of its type: t1 after Trinka 2015 (tonic-clonic 5 minutes, focal with impaired consciousness and absence 10 minutes), for convulsive seizures the usual duration plus 2 minutes when that comes first (NICE NG217), otherwise 5 minutes. Clusters are counted under your rule and under NICE (3 in 24 hours). The seizure types follow the ILAE 2025 classification."
          }
        },
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "De timer toont het noodplan zodra een aanval de drempel van zijn type bereikt: t1 volgens Trinka 2015 (tonisch-klonisch 5 minuten, focaal met verminderd bewustzijn en absence 10 minuten), bij convulsieve aanvallen de gebruikelijke duur plus 2 minuten als dat eerder is (NICE NG217), anders 5 minuten. Clusters worden geteld volgens jouw regel en volgens NICE (3 in 24 uur). De aanvalstypes volgen de ILAE-classificatie van 2025."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "타이머는 발작이 해당 유형의 기준에 도달하면 응급 계획을 보여 줘요. 기준은 Trinka 2015의 t1(강직간대 5분, 의식 저하를 동반한 국소 발작과 결신 10분), 경련성 발작은 평소 지속 시간에 2분을 더한 값이 더 이르면 그 값(NICE NG217), 그 밖에는 5분이에요. 군집 발작은 내 기준과 NICE 기준(24시간 내 3회)으로 세요. 발작 유형은 ILAE 2025 분류를 따라요."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needs_review",
            "value": "El cronómetro muestra el plan de emergencia cuando una crisis alcanza el umbral de su tipo: t1 según Trinka 2015 (tónico-clónica 5 minutos, focal con conciencia alterada y ausencia 10 minutos); en las crisis convulsivas, la duración habitual más 2 minutos si se alcanza antes (NICE NG217); si no, 5 minutos. Los racimos se cuentan según tu regla y según NICE (3 en 24 horas). Los tipos de crisis siguen la clasificación ILAE 2025."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "seizures.safety.header": {
      "comment": "Seizure diary: footer under the quick log (web seizures.safety.header, without the blanket disclaimer tail).",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "de": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dieser Kalender hält fest, was du beobachtest, damit du es mit dem Behandlungsteam teilen kannst. Im Notfall gilt der Plan, den ihr mit dem Behandlungsteam vereinbart habt."
          }
        },
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "This diary records what you observe so you can share it with the care team. In an emergency, follow the plan agreed with the care team."
          }
        },
        "nl": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dit dagboek legt vast wat je waarneemt, zodat je het met het behandelteam kunt delen. Volg in een noodgeval het plan dat met het behandelteam is afgesproken."
          }
        },
        "ko": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "이 일지는 관찰한 내용을 기록해 의료진과 공유할 수 있게 해 줘요. 응급 상황에서는 의료진과 정한 계획을 따르세요."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Este diario registra lo que observas para que puedas compartirlo con el equipo médico. En una emergencia, sigue el plan acordado con el equipo médico."
          }
        }
      }
    },
